# {{team.slug}}-kb-mcp — optional local stdio MCP server

This server is **optional and local-only**. Your primary coding client reads
this repo directly and does not need it. Enable it only if a **second** coding
client needs the same knowledge tools (`kb_search`, `kb_get`, `kb_manifest`,
`kb_coverage_gap`, `kb_freshness`).

## Enable it

1. `cd mcp-server && npm install`
2. Register it in your client's MCP config as a **stdio** server pointing at
   this `server.mjs`:

   ```json
   {
     "mcpServers": {
       "{{team.slug}}-kb": {
         "command": "node",
         "args": ["./mcp-server/server.mjs"]
       }
     }
   }
   ```

3. Restart the client. The five `kb_*` tools become available.

Every tool shells out to the `team-ai` CLI against this repo and is read-only.
The server imports none of the framework internals. Delete this directory if you
never add a second client.
